Overlay patch 0037 rev2: TextureCacheDelete releases the Metal texture
— and deliberately does NOT unload the CPU resource.

The flicker (rev1's correct half): TextureCacheDelete — the
gSPInvalidateTexCache path — recycled texture ids into free_texture_ids
WITHOUT DeleteTexture (review-P1-4 class, third site; count-evict fixed
in 0030 rev5, byte-evict in 0022). Luigi Raceway / Wario Stadium
invalidate their six 64x32 jumbotron tiles EVERY FRAME; the recycled ids
made re-imports replaceRegion MTLTextures still referenced by in-flight
draws (Metal samples at execution), so tiles showed each other's / stale
content: the user-reported jumbotron shimmer. Releasing here is safe:
encoders retain bound textures until the command buffer completes (same
argument as 0022's byte-evict, shipping since rev9).

The white-texture regression (rev1's fatal half, atticed 2026-07-22):
rev1 ALSO called UnloadResource on the entry's resource_path. But
TextureCacheDelete's targets are definitionally HOT — invalidated
because their CPU contents JUST changed and will re-import THIS frame.
The jumbotron tiles are live readback targets: the game writes each
frame's rear-view into the RESOURCE's own buffer through raw
LOAD_ASSET_RAW pointers (LuigiRaceway.cpp copy_framebuffer), then
invalidates by path. Unloading that resource mid-DL frees a buffer the
game still addresses (use-after-free writes) and makes every subsequent
by-path resolution (the invalidate middleware's LoadResource, the packed
DL's set-image resolution, next tick's LOAD_ASSET_RAW) re-load PRISTINE
ARCHIVE BYTES — severing the live-content pipeline and churning
alloc/free every frame. With the 4K pack loaded the churn and re-load
land in a heap full of MB-scale decode buffers: jumbotron and start-line
banners rendered solid white on device and sim. UnloadResource belongs
ONLY to eviction paths, where the LRU-front entry is cold by
construction (0022/0030). Mip-blit ordering was ruled out:
sSohIosPendingMips retains on push and EndFrame's blit tolerates deleted
entries by design (0021 rev4 comment); the bind-skip cache resets per
frame/encoder and command-buffer retains make a same-address false match
impossible within a frame.


--- a/libultraship/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
@@ -551,6 +551,24 @@
                         mRenderingState.mTextures[j] = nullptr;
                 }
                 mTextureCache.lru.erase(it->second.lru_location);
+#ifdef __IOS__
+                // SOH_IOS (overlay 0037 rev2): release the Metal texture BEFORE
+                // recycling the id — a recycled id reused at the same dims
+                // replaceRegions an MTLTexture that in-flight draws still
+                // reference (Metal samples at execution time); the jumbotron
+                // invalidates 6 tiles per frame and shimmered from exactly
+                // this aliasing (review-P1-4 class, third site). Safe: command
+                // buffers retain bound textures until completion.
+                // Deliberately NO UnloadResource here (rev1's white-texture
+                // regression): entries deleted here are HOT — invalidated
+                // because their CPU contents just changed and re-import THIS
+                // frame. The jumbotron writes its readback into the RESOURCE
+                // buffer via raw LOAD_ASSET_RAW pointers; unloading swaps the
+                // live-written buffer for pristine archive bytes mid-frame and
+                // frees memory the game still addresses. Unload only at
+                // eviction (cold LRU front, 0022/0030).
+                mRapi->DeleteTexture(it->second.texture_id);
+#endif
                 mTextureCache.free_texture_ids.push_back(it->second.texture_id);
                 mTextureCache.map.erase(it->first);
                 again = true;
